      trivia: "【Eight fires】The official family history states that the family's company suffered eight fires in all after its founding in 1912. Burned out in Tampa in 1924, in Nicaragua in 1978 and then in Honduras, it rose again each time — a record described as a “trial by fire”.\n【A one-dollar company】The price at which Carlos Sr. bought the company from his father in 1958 is officially told as “exactly one dollar”, a celebrated emblem of the generational handover.\n【The cigar that became a wristwatch】The Swiss luxury watchmaker Hublot has produced the collaborative Big Bang Unico Arturo Fuente with the family — a rare instance of a cigar brand becoming a subject of haute horlogerie."
