      trivia: "The spark was not a cigar but a book. The Gourmet Guide to Cigars, self-published in 1990 after seven years of research and two of writing, was researched largely inside Georgetown Tobacco, the venerable Washington, D.C. tobacconist, which then played midwife by selling the first PG line, completed in November of that year, exclusively in its own shop. At the boom's height the firm reached 300 accounts and 720,000 cigars a year, whereupon father and son stopped expanding; ever since, they have kept to a small operation with deep stocks and a policy of never saying “out of stock”. In September 2023 Garmirian published the memoir The Road to Cigars: A Memoir."
